      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/prague_zbraslav",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Zbraslav joined Prague in 1974, becoming part of the city’s 16th district alongside Lahovice.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/prague_zbraslav",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 1340s Madonna of Zbraslav, a Gothic tempera panel, was painted for the abbey’s chapel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zbraslav",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Zbraslav’s hills and riverbank parks stretch over 179 hectares along the Vltava–Berounka confluence.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/prague_zbraslav",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The former monastic brewery, still intact, dates back to the late‑baroque era and operated until 1950.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/prague_zbraslav",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Zbraslav was first mentioned in 1118, making it one of Prague’s oldest suburbs.",
